<title>Australia: RTRS-ACCC says agrees Weston starch buy.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ACCC says agrees Weston starch buy.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Competition and Consumer Commission (ACCC) said on Monday it would not intervene in the purchase by George Weston Foods Ltd of the Australian starch unit of the Latin American Bunge group.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the market is quite concentrated, and the proposed acquisition would reduce the number of domestic starch manufacturers from four to three, most customers did not express any concern about the acquisition,&quot; the ACCC said.</p>
<p>George Weston, 78 percent owned by Associated British Foods Plc, announced the purchase in November.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
